[{"q":"In a stampede, move ____ the crowd if you can, protect your chest.","options":["deeper into","sideways out of","by sitting in the middle","against blindly"],"answer":1,"explain":"Protect yourself; don’t push."},{"q":"When cycling, wear a ____.","options":["helmet","blindfold","long loose scarf in the wheel","earphones at full volume always"],"answer":0,"explain":"Helmets protect the head."},{"q":"When crossing the road, look ____, right and left again.","options":["at the sky only","backwards only","at your phone only","left"],"answer":3,"explain":"Stop, look and listen."},{"q":"Medicines at home should be kept ____.","options":["next to sweets","in drink bottles","out of children’s reach","on the floor"],"answer":2,"explain":"Wrong medicine is dangerous."},{"q":"A whistle can be used to ____ for help.","options":["iron","sweep","call","cook"],"answer":2,"explain":"Loud signals attract attention."},{"q":"Do not put ____ in sockets.","options":["fingers or metal","a charger the right way","nothing always including plugs","the plug of a safe appliance"],"answer":0,"explain":"Electric shock is dangerous."},{"q":"Report suspicious bags in public to ____.","options":["a stranger to open it","nobody","security / police","your younger sibling only"],"answer":2,"explain":"Do not touch unknown packages."},{"q":"School ID and visitors’ passes help to ____.","options":["play football","know who belongs","cook","decorate only"],"answer":1,"explain":"Visitors should report at the gate."},{"q":"The police emergency number often taught is ____.","options":["0000","12","7777","199"],"answer":3,"explain":"199 can reach the police."},{"q":"In a fire, ____ to the nearest exit.","options":["hide under a nylon bag","move quickly and calmly","go back for toys first always","use the lift in a burning house if told never"],"answer":1,"explain":"Know the escape route. Don’t use lifts in a fire."},{"q":"Security education teaches us to stay ____.","options":["silent in class always","afraid of everyone forever","away from school","safe"],"answer":3,"explain":"Be alert, not fearful."},{"q":"Do not take ____ given by friends without an adult’s knowledge.","options":["your own water bottle","a textbook","your own lunch","unknown drugs or tablets"],"answer":3,"explain":"Unknown substances can harm you."},{"q":"When the alarm rings, ____.","options":["lock yourself in the toilet always","follow emergency instructions","ignore it","run in any direction screaming only"],"answer":1,"explain":"Practise drills seriously."},{"q":"Your body is private. If someone touches you in a bad way, ____.","options":["blame yourself","hide at the market","keep silent forever","tell a trusted adult"],"answer":3,"explain":"It is not your fault. Speak up."},{"q":"The assembly point is where we ____ in an emergency.","options":["hide from teachers","play football first","buy snacks","meet"],"answer":3,"explain":"Schools have assembly points."},{"q":"A strong password should not be ____.","options":["secret","long","1234 or your name","a mix of letters and numbers"],"answer":2,"explain":"Guessable passwords are weak."},{"q":"Flood safety: do not walk in ____ water.","options":["a shallow known gutter at home never anyway wait","fast or deep","a bath","a puddle with an adult on the compound"],"answer":1,"explain":"Flood water can hide holes and germs."},{"q":"Wear a ____ in a car.","options":["seat belt","loose scarf on the door","blindfold","school bag on the head"],"answer":0,"explain":"Seat belts save lives."},{"q":"If you get lost in a market, ____.","options":["stay put and look for a security post / tell a seller with a stall to find police","follow any stranger home","hide in a boot of a car","leave town"],"answer":0,"explain":"Stay visible and ask official help."},{"q":"If a stranger asks you to go with them, you should ____.","options":["enter the car","keep it secret","follow quietly","say no and tell an adult"],"answer":3,"explain":"Never go with a stranger."},{"